<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Learn what information Cocoa & Kind collects for chocolate orders and how it is used."
  kicker="Your information, handled thoughtfully"
>
  <p>
    This draft explains how the sample shop's checkout is designed. Confirm the details and
    replace every bracketed prompt before publishing; have the final notice reviewed for the
    privacy laws that apply to your business and customers.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible for your information</h2>
  <p>
    The shop operator is <strong>[ADD FULL LEGAL BUSINESS OR OWNER NAME]</strong>, trading as
    Cocoa &amp; Kind. Privacy contact: <strong>[ADD PRIVACY OR CUSTOMER SUPPORT EMAIL]</strong>,
    <strong>[ADD BUSINESS ADDRESS]</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information used for an order</h2>
  <p>
    When you check out, the website asks for your name, phone number, delivery address, and
    optionally your email address. To calculate an approximate distance, the checkout also
    sends the delivery pin’s latitude and longitude to the shop’s Cloudflare Worker. The Worker
    calculates the straight-line distance and uses it to suggest Porter (15 km or less) or
    courier (over 15 km) for the shop to book manually. The shop’s site does not send the
    coordinates to an external geocoding or distance API or include them in Razorpay order notes.
    If you choose your device’s location, your browser or device’s location services may process
    location information under their own terms. Provide the delivery pin, rather than a different
    current location, so the estimate is useful.
  </p>
  <p>
    The checkout sends your contact and delivery details and the selected product and manual
    delivery-method details to the shop's Cloudflare Worker. The Worker creates a Razorpay order
    and includes the supplied contact and delivery address in that payment provider's order notes
    so the shop can fulfil the order. Provide only information needed to contact you and deliver
    your purchase.
  </p>
  <p>
    The shopping bag is saved in your browser's local storage so it can remain available when
    you return. This starter site does not set up advertising analytics or a separate customer
    database. Review the production hosting, application logs, and any services you add before
    publishing; update this notice if your actual practices differ.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Payments and service providers</h2>
  <p>
    Razorpay processes payment through its own checkout. This website does not collect or store
    your full card, bank, or payment credentials. Cloudflare runs the checkout Worker, and
    GitHub Pages hosts the static website. These providers may process information under their
    own terms and privacy notices. Add or update this list if the shop starts using email,
    analytics, customer-support, shipping, or other services that receive personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How the shop uses information</h2>
  <p>
    The intended use is to create and confirm payment orders, contact you about an order, arrange
    its delivery, and respond to a question or issue. Add the shop's accurate retention schedule,
    accounting or legal recordkeeping purposes, and any other use before publishing:
    <strong>[ADD ACTUAL RETENTION PERIODS AND ANY OTHER PURPOSES]</strong>. This starter site
    does not subscribe customers to marketing messages.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your privacy choices and requests</h2>
  <p>
    To ask about, correct, or request deletion of information, contact
    <strong>[ADD PRIVACY OR CUSTOMER SUPPORT EMAIL]</strong>. Add the rights available to
    customers, response process, and any applicable privacy authority contact after reviewing
    local requirements: <strong>[ADD APPLICABLE PRIVACY RIGHTS AND REQUEST PROCESS]</strong>.
    Some payment or accounting records may need to be retained when required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Security and children</h2>
  <p>
    Checkout uses a server-side Worker to keep Razorpay secret credentials out of the website's
    public code. No internet transmission or storage is entirely risk-free. Add the shop's
    contact and response steps for a suspected privacy incident:
    <strong>[ADD PRIVACY INCIDENT CONTACT OR PROCESS]</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Updates and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page if the shop's practices change. Effective date:
    <strong>[ADD EFFECTIVE DATE]</strong>. Privacy questions:
    <strong>[ADD PRIVACY OR CUSTOMER SUPPORT EMAIL AND POSTAL ADDRESS]</strong>.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
